     "title_type": "TV Series",
     "description": "For Life (2020) is an American crime and legal drama created by Hank Steinberg and inspired by the true story of Isaac Wright Jr. It stars Nicholas Pinnock as Aaron Wallace, a man wrongfully convicted who becomes a practicing lawyer while serving a life sentence, and features a supporting ensemble that brings the prison and courtroom worlds to life. Across its episodes, and directed by a team of television directors, the series blends courtroom procedure, serialized character arcs, and prison-set drama to chronicle Wallace’s efforts to overturn his conviction and to represent fellow inmates. The narrative explores systemic corruption, the moral complexities of legal advocacy, and the personal costs of incarceration, delivering a tense, emotionally charged tone that balances harrowing setbacks with moments of hard-won redemption.",
     "finale_year": 2021,
     "wikidata_id": "q65069236",
     "plot_summary": "A man serving a life sentence for a crime he did not commit trains himself in the law from behind bars and mounts a legal campaign to overturn his conviction while simultaneously representing other inmates. Working with limited resources and under constant institutional pressure, he becomes an inmate-attorney who navigates prison politics, prosecutorial resistance, and the complexities of courtroom procedure to expose corruption and new evidence. The story traces his strategic use of legal motions, investigation, and appeals alongside the personal costs of incarceration — strained family relationships, the day-to-day hardships of prison life, and the moral compromises required to survive and fight for justice.",
     "release_date": "2020-02-11",
     "release_year": 2020,
     "collaborators": [
      "Hank Steinberg",
      "Isaac Wright Jr.",
      "George Tillman, Jr.",
      "Alison Greenspan",
      "Curtis '50 Cent' Jackson",
      "Doug Robinson",
