     "title_type": "TV Series",
     "description": "All Rise (2019) is an ensemble legal drama starring Simone Missick, Wilson Bethel and Jessica Camacho that chronicles the personal and professional lives of judges, lawyers, clerks, bailiffs and police in an L.A. County courthouse. The series combines procedural court cases with character-focused storylines to examine ethical dilemmas, race and community impact. Praised for its diverse cast and emotional range, the show balances social commentary with moments of humor, heartbreak and moral complexity. Its tone is earnest and character-driven, inviting both emotional investment and discussion.",
     "finale_year": 2023,
     "wikidata_id": "q63965791",
     "plot_summary": "Set in an L.A. County courthouse, the series follows the intertwined personal and professional lives of judges, lawyers, clerks, bailiffs and police as they navigate trials, procedural pressures and ethical dilemmas. Each episode balances courtroom proceedings with scenes that reveal the characters' private struggles, relationships and moral choices. Storylines frequently intersect, exposing tensions between duty, justice and personal loyalty while offering social commentary on race and inequity. The ensemble format emphasizes how individual cases reverberate through both the legal system and the characters' home lives.",
